# Xcode build artifacts
build/
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcuserdatad/
xcuserdata/

# Generated Xcode project (regenerate via `xcodegen generate`)
# Per-developer Xcode state, which is the only genuinely generated noise inside
# the project bundle. The bundle itself is NOT blanket-ignored, and that is a
# deliberate correction.
#
# `*.xcodeproj/` used to sit here. It swept up
# project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/Package.resolved, the SPM lockfile,
# which is not generated: it is the resolved dependency graph. Two consequences,
# both real. Every clean build resolved fresh, so a dependency change was
# invisible in review, with no iOS equivalent of the backend's
# --frozen-lockfile guarantee. And the `swift` Dependabot entry added in #259
# had nothing to read, so it could never open a PR. That PR claimed every
# ecosystem was now watched. For Swift it was not.
#
# Note that a blanket rule could not simply be negated: git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded, so the fix has to be a narrower
# ignore rather than an exception to a broad one.
*.xcodeproj/**/xcuserdata/
*.xcworkspace/**/xcuserdata/
*.xcworkspace/

# SPM artifacts
.swiftpm/
.build/
Packages/

# Test artifacts
*.xcresult

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Fastlane
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
fastlane/screenshots
fastlane/test_output
